{
  "rationale": "This is the final round, so the only valid choices are stop or infeasible. The spec is satisfiable: 52 of 60 evaluations are feasible, and the throughput constraint is met by every design (0% violate, best 10.1 MSPS vs >=1 required) while the error constraint is met by the whole Pareto front (best 2^-24.34 vs <=2^-10 required). The front already spans the objectives well: area_um2 7106..23735 against the HV reference 40000, and accuracy_bits 10.2..24.3 against the HV reference 10, with data_width 15..28 covering most of the registry range. The selection rule (min area_um2) is satisfied by iterative [data_width=15 n_iter=15 angle_guard=0 frac_guard=1 rounding=trunc] at area_um2=7106, accuracy_bits=10.2, max_abs_err=0.000822 (2^-10.25), throughput 7.86 MSPS — comfortably inside both constraints. No further round is available to improve the front, and no constraint is unreachable, so stopping is correct rather than declaring infeasible.",
  "next_plan": null,
  "decision": "stop"
